t_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"take the example at https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/master/examples/extending_query/filter_public.py and add at the bottom:\r\n\r\n```\r\n     sess.refresh(u1)\r\n```\r\n\r\n`it fails because the event handler is adding WHERE criteria such that the row can't be located.\r\n\r\nadditionally the criteria options continue to compound each other when a refresh is used, because we take the existing options in the state and send them through again, strongly suggesting this handler should be excluded from these queries by default:\r\n\r\n```\r\n    u2 = sess.execute(select(User).filter(User.name == \"u2\")).scalar_one()\r\n    sess.refresh(u2)\r\n\r\n    sess.refresh(u2)\r\n\r\n    sess.refresh(u2)\r\n```\r\n\r\nproducing:\r\n\r\n```\r\nSELECT user.public, user.id, user.name \r\nFROM user \r\nWHERE user.id = ? AND user.public = 1 AND user.public = 1 AND user.public = 1\r\n\r\n```\r\n\r\nat the very least we need an ORMExecuteState flag and I think perhaps we should make this event require flags to indicate what operations are desired, that is:\r\n\r\n```\r\n@event.listens_for(Session, \"do_orm_execute\", normal_selects=True, relationship_loads=False)\r\ndef _add_filtering_criteria(execute_state):\r\n\r\n```\r\n\r\nif no flags are given, an error is raised.   user has to opt in positively to all events.","closed_by":{"login":"sqlalchemy-bot","id":36047385,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2MDQ3Mzg1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/36047385?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot","html_url":"https://github.com/sqlalchemy-bot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.c